  "goodToKnow": "Das Wahlrecht is both the right to vote and the electoral law. Das aktive Wahlrecht is the right to vote, das passive Wahlrecht the right to stand for election. German women gained the vote in November 1918 and first voted in January 1919. Voting age for the Bundestag is 18, but some states let 16-year-olds vote in local and state elections. A 2023 Wahlrechtsreform aimed to shrink the oversized Bundestag to 630 seats."
